  "name": null,
  "problem": "The velocity of the particle in the $y$-direction when $t=1$ is equal to the rate of change of the particle's $y$-coordinate at this time. Calculate this velocity.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The velocity of the particle in the $y$-direction when $t=1$ second equals\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The rate of change of the particle's $y$-coordinate when $t=1$ is given by ${y}^{\u2032}(1).$\n\nIn step 5, we found that\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}(t)=\\frac{6-12{t}^{2}}{2{t}^{3}+3t}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032}(1) & =\\frac{6-12(1)^{2}}{2(1)^{3}+3(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-12}{2+3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{5}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
